From af5378f2097dfe4c761f3005e515fee9c132f5b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: letress <212964567+letress@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:36:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 05/17] arm64: dts: exynos9610: Fix misspelled
 samsung,pin-pud/pin-drv properties

53 pin configuration properties in the FSYS and TOP pin controllers are
spelled with a dot instead of a comma ("samsung.pin-pud",
"samsung.pin-drv"). The pinctrl driver looks up "samsung,pin-pud" and
"samsung,pin-drv", so the pull and drive strength settings of these pin
groups (sd0, sd1, i2c, uart, spi, ...) are silently ignored, and
dtbs_check fails on every affected node:

  pinctrl@13490000: sd0-clk-pins: 'samsung.pin-drv' does not match any
  of the regexes: '^pinctrl-[0-9]+$'

Use the documented property names.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
